# The Railway project is declared as code in .railway/railway.ts (see PLAN.md → Deployment).
# Most variables come from there automatically, so they are NOT set by hand:
#   DATABASE_URL / REDIS_URL  → references to the Postgres / Redis resources
#   GCS_PROJECT / GCS_BUCKET  → constants in railway.ts
#   PORT=3000                 → so Railway routes + healthchecks the port Puma binds (/up)
#
# Only the two SECRETS are set manually: railway.ts holds them via preserve() (kept out of
# source), so set them ONCE on the `web` service — the worker references web's copy:
#
#   railway variables --service web --set-from-stdin RAILS_MASTER_KEY < config/master.key
#   railway variables --service web --set-from-stdin GCS_KEYFILE_JSON < ~/.config/gcloud-keys/<key>.json
#
# (Redis defaults to maxmemory-policy=noeviction, which Sidekiq requires.)

RAILS_MASTER_KEY=<contents of config/master.key>
GCS_KEYFILE_JSON=<service-account key JSON, single line>
